//! Asset classes are separate from the Rails catalogue's sync-routing `assets.category`.
//! D-ASSET-TAXONOMY: a legacy Cryptocurrency row can be a stablecoin or RWA. Do not rewrite
//! that routing column: the catalogue importer and venue sweeps still use it.
//!
//! CategoryOverride is the local authority, before the provider's classification. This registry
//! covers the bundled catalogue generated by `rake seed:generate` (lib/tasks/seed.rake);
//! its coverage/hash guard is bundled_stablecoin_classification_grid in tests/index.rs.
//! Review the registry when that generator changes the catalogue. No symbol/name/price heuristic.
//!
//! Sources: https://www.coingecko.com/en/categories/stablecoins (including pages 2–4),
//! https://www.coingecko.com/en/coins/quantoz-usdq, https://schuman.io/,
//! https://usdhl.xyz/, https://www.coingecko.com/en/coins/usdt0.
//! USD Mapped Token audit: https://wp.hacken.io/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Hacken_USDM_USDM-LOC_-104_P-2023-052_3_20231219-15_31.pdf
//! Gold and treasury wrappers are RWA,
//! overriding CoinGecko's broader commodity-backed stablecoin grouping.

#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum AssetClass { Crypto, Stablecoin, Rwa, Stock, Etf, Fiat }

pub struct CategoryOverride { pub external_id: &'static str, pub class: AssetClass }

